course: dictionary
lesson: 4332
title: Feelings as nouns
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noun names a thing, and many feelings can be nouns too. Grumpiness is a noun. It names the state of being grumpy, which means being in a bad, cross mood and easily annoyed. Grumpy becomes grumpiness, just as happy becomes happiness.
explain: Grumpiness is uncountable, so we do not say "a grumpiness" or "two grumpinesses". We say "some grumpiness" or "a lot of grumpiness". Grumpy is the adjective, and grumpily is the adverb, as in "He grumbled grumpily".
explain: Context often shows you the cause. «Hunger shows as a rumbling tummy, low energy, grumpiness and trouble paying attention.» The clues are tummy and energy, so grumpiness is a cross mood caused by being hungry. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
fact: «Grumpiness» means the state of being grumpy: a bad, cross mood where you are easily annoyed.
fact: Tiredness, hunger and illness often cause grumpiness, and a snack, rest or a kind word can help.
fact: «Sudden grumpiness is often a sign of pain» in a pet, so tell an adult, who can take the pet to a vet.
fact: In stories, a grumpy character's grumpiness often melts away by the end.
fact: Grumpiness is uncountable, so write "some grumpiness", not "a grumpiness".
exercise: «Hunger shows as a rumbling tummy, low energy and grumpiness.» What is grumpiness? | Being very tall for your age | Happiness after a big meal | *The state of being in a bad, cross mood | Sleeping very deeply
exercise: Which word is the adverb that goes with grumpy? | grumble | grumpiness | grumpy-hat | *grumpily
exercise: Tiredness is making you grumpy. What can help the grumpiness? | Staying up later | Skipping lunch | *A snack or a rest | Shouting louder at everyone
test: Which sentence uses grumpiness correctly? | She felt a grumpiness after lunch. | *She felt some grumpiness after lunch. | She felt grumpily after lunch. | She felt grumpinesses after lunch.
test: «Saying "I was wrong" quickly saves time and grumpiness.» What does saying sorry quickly do? | *Saves time and stops the grumpiness | Makes the grumpiness grow | Starts a long argument | Turns grumpiness into a noun
exam: A pet shows sudden grumpiness. What should you do? | Ignore it, it will pass | Laugh at it and carry on | Give it more sugar | *Tell an adult, as it can be a sign of pain
